# Dockle checkpoints suppressed for this image.
#
# mcvs-docker-action runs goodwithtech/dockle-action at its default
# `exit-level: warn`, so only WARN and FATAL checkpoints can fail the build;
# INFO ones are printed and ignored. That is why this list is short — see the
# "deliberately not listed" note at the bottom.
#
# The action already hardcodes `--ignore CIS-DI-0005,CIS-DI-0006`, so those two
# must not be repeated here.

# CIS-DI-0001 (WARN) "Create a user for the container".
# Reported as "Last user should not be root", and that is deliberate. The
# container starts as root so entrypoint.sh can chown /root to the host UID and
# useradd a matching passwd entry, then drops privileges via runuser;
# --security-opt no-new-privileges rules out a file-capability workaround.
# Steady state, claude runs as the host user with no effective, permitted or
# ambient capabilities — the kernel clears those on the UID -> non-zero
# transition, and the bounding set is inert under no-new-privileges. Adding a
# USER directive would break the entrypoint's chown; the Dockerfile carries the
# same rationale above WORKDIR and explicitly forbids one.
# See entrypoint.sh and run.sh's --cap-add lines for the full picture.
CIS-DI-0001

# DKL-DI-0005 (FATAL) "Clear apt-get caches".
# Fires on the glab layer, which apt-get installs a locally downloaded .deb and
# then removes only the .deb, not /var/lib/apt/lists. Dockle trips on `apt-get
# install` OR `apt-get update` and then wants `rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists/*` in a
# later &&-segment of the same RUN. Installing a local .deb never populates
# /var/lib/apt/lists (no apt-get update precedes it, and the preceding layer
# already emptied the directory), so there is nothing to clear — a false
# positive against this Dockerfile. Note hadolint's DL3009 keys on `apt-get
# update` alone, which is why this same layer passes hadolint and fails dockle.
# Remove this line once that RUN gains the cleanup anyway (see PR follow-ups).
DKL-DI-0005

# Deliberately NOT listed. Both are INFO, so they do not gate at
# exit-level=warn, and suppressing them would only hide signal:
#   CIS-DI-0008  setuid/setgid files inherited from the base image
#                (mount, su, passwd, chsh, gpasswd, ssh-keysign, ...)
#   DKL-LI-0003  deletable files — tfenv's bundled /opt/tfenv/Dockerfile
#                and root/.npm
